\DOC ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC : term -> term -> term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Reduces an {ensures} goal about a whole program whose postcondition event trace
is built from a prologue, an {ENUMERATEL}-style iterated loop body and an
epilogue to a single conjunctive goal: a non-triviality side condition together
with three {ensures} subproblems for loop entry, a generic iteration, and loop
exit.

\DESCRIBE
The arguments are four terms: {k}, the iteration count (a numeral or an
arithmetic term), used both as the loop bound and as the index at which the
loop trace is complete; {pc1}, the loop head address, i.e. the postcondition
program counter of the entry step and of an iteration that is not the last;
{pc2}, the loop exit address, i.e. the program counter reached by the final
iteration and assumed at the start of the exit step; and {loop_inv}, a function
of the iteration index and the machine state giving the state part of the loop
invariant, instantiated at {0}, at a variable {i}, at {i + 1} and at {k}.
{
            A ?- t
     ============================  ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC k pc1 pc2 loop_inv
            A ?- u
}
\noindent Here {t} is an {ensures} statement and {u} is a conjunction of four
parts: {~(k = 0)}; an {ensures} with the original precondition and a
postcondition formed from the loop head address, {loop_inv} at index {0}, and
the trace being the prologue extended by the enumerated body up to {0}; a
universally quantified iteration goal {forall i. i < k /\ ~(i = k) /\ ~(k = 0)
/\ 0 < k ==> ensures ...} whose pre- and postconditions use {loop_inv} at {i}
and at {i + 1}, with the post program counter written as a conditional choosing
the loop head or the exit address according to whether {i + 1 < k}, and the
trace growing from index {i} to {i + 1}; and an {ensures} from the exit address
with {loop_inv} at {k} and the completed loop trace to the original
postcondition. The frame ({MAYCHANGE} component) of the original goal is reused
in each of the three {ensures} conjuncts.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal transformation, applied to
{ensures} goals whose postcondition trace already has the
prologue/enumerated-body/epilogue shape.

\ENDDOC
